{
  "about": "What the native decoder must reproduce (#264): the RGB16 SHA-256 of libraw-wasm's deterministic rebuild (LibRaw 0.22.1, no fast-math, -ffp-contract=off, musl 1.2.6 libm; #264 part B, libraw-wasm branch perf229-264 @ 14af432, not released yet), identical for its single-threaded build and its threaded build at 1-8 threads, and the metadata(true) fields the page reads. Hashes are over imageData().data (width*height*3 native-endian uint16) with rawFileLoader.js's options, outputBps 16; halfRgb16 with halfSize. `metadata` is the worker's metadata(true) object before index.js post-processes thumb_format, desc and timestamp, restricted to the keys the native object has (native_raw.rs RawMetadata); libraw-wasm 1.6.0 and the deterministic build report the same values for every file here. The HE-compressed NEFs have no hashes: LibRaw cannot decode them; their `embeddedPreview` is what the app's loader falls back to, the embedded JPEG at 1703835 (SHA-256 of the 8-bit plane decoded by Chrome), which the WASM RGB16 gate holds (scripts/raw-decode-gate-smoke.mjs, `--raw-decode-gate-only`). Files are matched by name and size; the camera files are not in the repository.",
